OL,3,AMiliband says slavery apology will not
OL,4,Abring cost for UK taxpayers
OL,5,
OL,6,FForeign Secretary Ed Miliband has
OL,7,Finsisted the government's willingness
OL,8,Fto consider formally apologising for
OL,9,Fthe UK's role in the transatlantic
OL,10,Fslave trade will not lead to higher
OL,11,Fcosts for the British taxpayer.
OL,13,FThe prime minister has said the UK will
OL,14,Fnot pay reparations to affected
OL,15,Fcountries, but declined to say whether
OL,16,Fhis new approach could involve
OL,17,Fadditional taxpayer money.
OL,23,APub: 04-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
